---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Fix Sinking Rock Guide', url: '/how-to-fix-rock-sinking-into-soil' }
];

const title = "Why Landscape Rock Sinks into Soil & How to Fix It - Remediation Guide";
const metaDescription = "Diagnose and fix landscape rock, river pebbles, and gravel sinking into muddy ground. Geotechnical subgrade failure causes, geotextile CBR puncture rules, and 4 practical fixes.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} metaDescription={metaDescription} canonicalPath="/how-to-fix-rock-sinking-into-soil">
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <PageHero
      title="Why Landscape Rock Sinks into Mud & How to Fix It"
      subtitle="Heavy stone laid directly over bare dirt will sink into the subgrade within 1 to 2 seasons. Understand the geotechnical root cause and learn 4 practical ways to fix sinking gravel."
      badge="Geotechnical Troubleshooting"
      breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
      theme="utility"
    />

    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="container">
        <!-- Diagnosis Summary Box -->
        <div class="aeo-box">
          <div class="aeo-header">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
            <h3>The Root Cause: Subgrade Shear Failure</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            When heavy rock (weighing 100 to 110 lbs per cubic foot) is poured onto native soil without an engineered geotextile separation barrier, three forces cause it to disappear: <strong>(1) Rainwater saturation</strong> softens the soil's California Bearing Ratio (CBR); <strong>(2) Point-load ground pressure</strong> forces sharp stone edges downward; and <strong>(3) Earthworm and biological activity</strong> pushes loose muddy castings upward over the stones. Within 18 months, your expensive rock bed turns into a lumpy, muddy weed patch.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 4 Remediation Fixes -->
        <div class="methods-container" style="margin-top: var(--space-10);">
          <article class="method-card">
            <div class="method-num-badge">Method 1</div>
            <div class="method-content">
              <h3>The "Scrape and Underlay" (Permanent Gold-Standard Fix)</h3>
              <p>
                If your rock is sinking in a decorative bed or pathway, temporary surface patches will only waste money. The permanent fix:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Use a flat-edge transfer shovel or landscape rake to scrape the top stone into temporary staging piles or wheelbarrows.</li>
                <li>Rake the muddy subsoil flat and compact it using a hand tamper.</li>
                <li>Lay a high-tensile <strong>4 oz to 6 oz Non-Woven or Class 1 Woven Geotextile Fabric</strong> (ASTM D4833 CBR puncture tested &gt; 300 lbs). Overlap all seams by at least <strong>12 inches</strong> and anchor with 6-inch steel landscape staples.</li>
                <li>Shovel the cleaned stone back over the fabric at the recommended <strong>3-inch minimum depth</strong>.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="method-tip">
                <strong>Why Cheap Landscape Fabric Fails:</strong> Standard thin spunbonded plastic weed barrier from hardware stores has a puncture resistance under 40 lbs. The first person who steps on a sharp rock drives it straight through the fabric like a nail.
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="method-card">
            <div class="method-num-badge">Method 2</div>
            <div class="method-content">
              <h3>The "Bridging Base Course" (For Driveways &amp; Parking Areas)</h3>
              <p>
                On vehicular surfaces, sinking rock is caused by tire shear loads. If you cannot remove all existing sunken gravel:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Do not add more clean river rock or pea gravel—it will simply sink deeper into the mud.</li>
                <li>Instead, spread a <strong>3- to 4-inch layer of Crusher Run (21-A / CA-6 dense aggregate base)</strong> directly over the existing sunken stone.</li>
                <li>The angular stones and mineral stone dust will lock into the sunken gravel voids, creating a rigid bridging slab that distributes vehicle tire loads across a wider surface area.</li>
                <li>Compact with a heavy vibratory plate compactor or roller while lightly misting with water.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="method-cta">
                <a href="/crusher-run-calculator" class="btn btn-sm btn-secondary">Calculate Crusher Run Base Volume &rarr;</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="method-card">
            <div class="method-num-badge">Method 3</div>
            <div class="method-content">
              <h3>Install Biaxial Geogrid Over Wet Clay (Tensioned Membrane Effect)</h3>
              <p>
                In areas with expansive high-plasticity clay soil (common in the Midwest, Texas, and the South), saturated subsoil turns into liquid mud during spring rains:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Roll out a <strong>Biaxial Geogrid (rigid polypropylene polymer mesh)</strong>.</li>
                <li>When crushed stone aggregate is dumped and compacted over the grid, the stone particles lock into the open aperture squares.</li>
                <li>This creates an interlocked "geosynthetic-reinforced mattress" that prevents rocks from being pushed down into the clay, acting like a snowshoe on soft powder snow.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="method-card">
            <div class="method-num-badge">Method 4</div>
            <div class="method-content">
              <h3>Subgrade Drainage &amp; Perforated Collector Pipes (Remove the Water)</h3>
              <p>
                Soil only liquefies and loses its bearing strength when saturated with trapped water. If water has nowhere to drain, the soil beneath your rock bed remains soft mud year-round:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Ensure the excavation subgrade is graded with a <strong>1% to 2% slope</strong> away from your home's foundation.</li>
                <li>If the area forms a low spot or natural basin, install a perforated French drain collector trench at the lowest edge.</li>
                <li>Draining subsurface pore water keeps the underlying clay firm and compacted, physically preventing stones from sinking.</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="method-cta">
                <a href="/drain-rock-calculator" class="btn btn-sm btn-secondary">Calculate Drain Rock for Drainage Remediation &rarr;</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <!-- Fabric Selection Table -->
        <div class="section-header" style="margin-top: var(--space-12);">
          <h2>Geotextile Underlayment Comparison Guide</h2>
          <div class="section-divider"></div>
          <p>Choosing the correct fabric specification is the #1 factor preventing future rock sinkage.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-table-card">
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="fabric-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Fabric Classification</th>
                  <th>CBR Puncture Strength</th>
                  <th>Water Permeability</th>
                  <th>Recommended Use Case</th>
                  <th>Will Rock Sink Through It?</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Cheap Spunbonded Plastic</strong></td>
                  <td>&lt; 50 lbs (Very Low)</td>
                  <td>Poor (Puddles)</td>
                  <td>Temporary annual flower beds only</td>
                  <td><span class="badge-fails">Yes, within 6 months</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>4 oz Non-Woven Geotextile</strong></td>
                  <td>250–350 lbs (High)</td>
                  <td>Excellent (High GPM)</td>
                  <td>Landscape garden beds, river rock, French drains</td>
                  <td><span class="badge-passes">No, 15+ year barrier</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Class 1 Woven Stabilization Fabric</strong></td>
                  <td>400–700 lbs (Extreme)</td>
                  <td>Moderate</td>
                  <td>Vehicular driveways, gravel roads, paver subbases</td>
                  <td><span class="badge-passes">Never (Truck load rated)</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Biaxial Geogrid Mesh</strong></td>
                  <td>Tensile Aperture Lock</td>
                  <td>100% Free Flow</td>
                  <td>Severe wet clay subgrades, parking pads</td>
                  <td><span class="badge-passes">Locks stone into grid</span></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Related Troubleshooting & Engineering Guides -->
        <div style="margin-top: 3.5rem; padding-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Related Problem-Solving Guides &amp; Tools</h2>
          <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
            <a href="/how-to-stop-weeds-in-landscape-rock" style="background: var(--slate-900); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem; text-decoration: none; display: block;">
              <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15); color: var(--accent-emerald); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px;">Weed Prevention</span>
              <h4 style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.05rem;">Stop Weeds in Landscape Rock</h4>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5;">Why weeds germinate above fabric in windblown silt and how flame weeders &amp; pre-emergents stop them.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/how-to-stop-gravel-washing-out-on-slope" style="background: var(--slate-900); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem; text-decoration: none; display: block;">
              <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.15); color: #eab308; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px;">Erosion Fix</span>
              <h4 style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.05rem;">Stop Gravel Washing Out on Slopes</h4>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5;">Angular stone interlocking, check dams, and geocell stabilization methods for erosion.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/rock-vs-mulch-calculator" style="background: var(--slate-900); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem; text-decoration: none; display: block;">
              <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: rgba(212, 168, 83, 0.15); color: var(--gold-400); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px;">Economic Model</span>
              <h4 style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.05rem;">Rock vs Mulch 10-Year Calculator</h4>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5;">Calculate the exact 3.4-year break-even point when rock beats recurring mulch costs.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/rock-bag-weight-and-price-guide" style="background: var(--slate-900); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem; text-decoration: none; display: block;">
              <span style="display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15); color: var(--accent-blue); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 6px;">Retail Pricing</span>
              <h4 style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.05rem;">Bag Weight &amp; Price Database</h4>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5;">Home Depot &amp; Lowe's 0.5 cu ft bag weights, payload safety, and bulk cost tipping points.</p>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .aeo-box {
    background: rgba(20, 26, 33, 0.7);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  .aeo-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    color: #f87171;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .aeo-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .aeo-box p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .methods-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .method-card {
    background: var(--slate-900);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  .method-num-badge {
    background: rgba(212, 168, 83, 0.15);
    border: 1px solid rgba(212, 168, 83, 0.3);
    color: var(--gold-400);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .method-content {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .method-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0;
  }

  .method-content p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  .method-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .method-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .method-tip {
    background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .method-tip strong {
    color: #f87171;
  }

  .method-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* Table */
  .fabric-table-card {
    background: var(--slate-900);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl);
  }

  .table-responsive {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .fabric-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .fabric-table th {
    background: var(--slate-850);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .fabric-table td {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(107, 122, 141, 0.15);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .fabric-table tr:hover td {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  }

  .badge-fails {
    color: #f87171;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .badge-passes {
    color: #34d399;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
